What's funny about Cylon toast?

269
00:12:29,230 --> 00:12:30,530
It's open.

270
00:12:31,830 --> 00:12:33,800
Hey, pal.

271
00:12:35,030 --> 00:12:36,900
What do you want?

272
00:12:36,960 --> 00:12:38,700
I brought you a little gift.

273
00:12:38,760 --> 00:12:41,430
New kite.

274
00:12:41,500 --> 00:12:45,400
The kite you made me lose was an authentic Patang,

275
00:12:45,460 --> 00:12:46,700
Indian fighting kite

276
00:12:46,760 --> 00:12:48,430
that my brother sent to me from New Delhi.

277
00:12:48,500 --> 00:12:51,430
It took me a day to put together and two days to paint.

278
00:12:51,500 --> 00:12:54,030
This is Hello Kitty.

279
00:12:56,360 --> 00:12:59,860
Yeah, but it comes with a little coin purse.

280
00:12:59,930 --> 00:13:01,830
Does a Patang?

281
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:04,430
Wow, you just don't get it, do you?

282
00:13:04,500 --> 00:13:06,230
Buying me something pretty isn't going

283
00:13:06,300 --> 00:13:10,100
to make our problem just go away.

284
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:12,100
Look, I admit I haven't always been

285
00:13:12,160 --> 00:13:13,700
the best friend I could be.

286
00:13:13,760 --> 00:13:16,900
You've been a sucky friend, a sucky, sucky friend.

287
00:13:17,960 --> 00:13:19,300
Stipulated.

288
00:13:19,360 --> 00:13:19,800
And you do it all the time.

289
00:13:20,730 --> 00:13:21,660
Last week in the mall at Radio Shack, we were looking

290
00:13:21,730 --> 00:13:24,730
for a phone with giant numbers for your mother,

291
00:13:24,900 --> 00:13:27,100
and I suddenly realize you're not even there.

292
00:13:27,100 --> 00:13:29,730
- I know, I know... - And Where were you?

293
00:13:29,730 --> 00:13:31,360
Getting shot down by the girl at Hot Dog on a Stick.

294
00:13:33,130 --> 00:13:35,600
But in my defense, she was gorgeous!

295
00:13:35,600 --> 00:13:37,870
And working that squeezer to make the lemonade,

296
00:13:37,870 --> 00:13:39,660
going and down and up and down.

297
00:13:41,300 --> 00:13:43,200
It was like a free pole dance

298
00:13:43,260 --> 00:13:45,800
right in the middle of the food court.

299
00:13:45,860 --> 00:13:47,360
You're impossible.

300
00:13:47,430 --> 00:13:49,960
Hey, at least I can talk to women

301
00:13:50,030 --> 00:13:51,460
without being drunk.

302
00:13:51,530 --> 00:13:53,660
Excuse me, I have selective mutism,

303
00:13:53,730 --> 00:13:55,730
a recognized medical disorder.

304
00:13:55,800 --> 00:13:57,960
You're just a douche.

305
00:13:59,130 --> 00:14:00,360
No. You know what?

306
00:14:00,430 --> 00:14:02,230
Maybe that's what this whole thing's about.

307
00:14:02,300 --> 00:14:03,330
You're not mad at me,

308
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:04,600
you're mad at yourself.

309
00:14:04,660 --> 00:14:05,960
No, I'm mad at you.

310
00:14:06,030 --> 00:14:08,400
I hate myself, but I'm mad at you.

311
00:14:09,460 --> 00:14:10,930
Fine. You're mad at me. I get it.

312
00:14:12,680 --> 00:14:15,280
How about we go spend the day together?

313
00:14:15,280 --> 00:14:17,060
Just the two of us.

314
00:14:17,060 --> 00:14:18,510
We'll go anywhere you want.

315
00:14:20,130 --> 00:14:21,260
I don't know.

316
00:14:21,260 --> 00:14:23,400
Come on.

317
00:14:24,160 --> 00:14:26,620
Let me take you someplace nice.

318
00:14:30,670 --> 00:14:33,790
I-I do enjoy the La Brea Tar Pits.

319
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:38,170
Really, now? With the traffic and the parking?

320
00:14:38,610 --> 00:14:40,380
Okay, fine.

321
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:42,250
The Tar Pits. Let's go.

322
00:14:46,360 --> 00:14:49,790
Oh, why can't I stay mad at you?

323
00:14:54,630 --> 00:14:56,000
Go! Go! Go!

324
00:14:56,060 --> 00:14:57,760
Go-go-go-go! Yes!

325
00:14:58,200 --> 00:14:59,200
Are you people watching this?

326
00:14:59,260 --> 00:15:01,030
Is this amazing or what?

327
00:15:02,100 --> 00:15:02,760
Sweetie, that's a highlight

328
00:15:02,830 --> 00:15:05,300
from the '98 championship game.

329
00:15:05,560 --> 00:15:08,630
Oh. Did not know that.

330
00:15:09,500 --> 00:15:11,630
- How much beer have you had? - None, why?

331
00:15:11,850 --> 00:15:14,100
Oh. I was just kind of hoping you were drunk.

332
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:17,430
- Now we're back live. - Okay, yeah.

333
00:15:17,700 --> 00:15:19,130
I can see the difference.

334
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:22,810
Oh, where's the flag? That's intentional grounding.

335
00:15:22,810 --> 00:15:25,870
- Totally. - That completely was a forward pass,

336
00:15:25,870 --> 00:15:27,780
Which they threw intentionally incomplete

337
00:15:27,780 --> 00:15:31,000
To avoid loss of yardage or to conserve time

338
00:15:31,360 --> 00:15:32,990
I can't believe they're not

339
00:15:32,990 --> 00:15:35,210
Being penalized with the loss of a down

340
00:15:35,210 --> 00:15:37,030
And by having to move the line of scrimmage

341
00:15:37,100 --> 00:15:39,800
Back to the spot of the foul.

342
00:15:41,660 --> 00:15:44,200
Here, have some pizza, sweetie.

343
00:15:44,260 --> 00:15:45,830
Penny, you know I'm lactose intolerant.

344
00:15:45,900 --> 00:15:48,160
I know. I just need you  stop talking.

345
00:15:49,560 --> 00:15:53,360
Penny. Penny. Penny.

346
00:15:54,700 --> 00:15:56,700
- Sheldon, come in. - Thank you.

347
00:15:56,760 --> 00:16:00,500
I'd like to make a sandwich, but I'm out of bread.

348
00:16:00,560 --> 00:16:03,230
There's some in the fridge.

349
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:05,060
You shouldn't keep your bread in the refrigerator.

350
00:16:05,130 --> 00:16:08,560
Staleness is caused by crystallization of the starch molecules,

351
00:16:08,560 --> 00:16:11,030
Which occurs faster at cool temperatures.

352
00:16:11,100 --> 00:16:13,600
On Earth, we say "thank you."

353
00:16:13,660 --> 00:16:16,730
So Leonard, how goes the mimesis?

354
00:16:16,800 --> 00:16:18,230
"Mimesis"?

355
00:16:18,300 --> 00:16:21,460
You know. Mimesis.

356
00:16:21,530 --> 00:16:24,760
An action in which the mimic takes on the properties

357
00:16:24,830 --> 00:16:27,530
of a specific object or organism.

358
00:16:27,600 --> 00:16:29,560
Mimesis.

359
00:16:31,200 --> 00:16:33,330
What the hell are you talking about?

360
00:16:33,400 --> 00:16:35,960
I'm attempting to communicate with you

361
00:16:36,030 --> 00:16:39,830
Without my meaning becoming apparent to those around you.

362
00:16:40,500 --> 00:16:42,410
Let me try again.

363
00:16:42,360 --> 00:16:46,330
Have the indigenous fauna

364
00:16:46,330 --> 00:16:48,630
Accepted you as one of their own?

365
00:16:48,630 --> 00:16:51,690
Nudge, nudge, wink, wink.

366
00:16:52,800 --> 00:16:54,630
Oh, I guess so.

367
00:16:54,630 --> 00:16:56,690
Good. Oh, FYI.

368
00:16:56,690 --> 00:16:59,500
After I eat my sandwich, I'm taking Koothrappali's

369
00:16:59,500 --> 00:17:01,260
Patang kite out for a test run.

370
00:17:01,260 --> 00:17:04,030
Would you like to get your delta-wing raptor and join me?

371
00:17:04,030 --> 00:17:05,670
I don't want to fly kites, Sheldon.

372
00:17:05,670 --> 00:17:07,990
We're watching football here.

373
00:17:07,990 --> 00:17:09,340
I can see that.

374
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:11,430
I was providing you with an alternative.

375
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:15,730
A courtesy I was never offered in similar circumstances.

376
00:17:18,430 --> 00:17:19,660
Oh, look at that.

377
00:17:19,930 --> 00:17:21,850
The Oklahoma coach throw down a red flag

378
00:17:21,850 --> 00:17:23,910
Indicating he's challenging the ruling on the field.

379
00:17:24,130 --> 00:17:26,100
I hope he's right, 'cause if he'not,

380
00:17:26,160 --> 00:17:28,000
It'll cost him one of his three time-outs.

381
00:17:33,560 --> 00:17:35,780
You know, Leonard, honey,

382
00:17:35,780 --> 00:17:39,740
I wouldn't mind if you wanted to go fly kites with Sheldon.

383
00:17:39,740 --> 00:17:41,560
No, I'll watch the end of the game.

384
00:17:41,630 --> 00:17:42,930
Besides, there's only three minutes left.

385
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:44,330
Until halftime.

386
00:17:44,400 --> 00:17:46,000
This is justalf?

387
00:17:47,200 --> 00:17:48,900
We've been here for hours.

388
00:17:48,960 --> 00:17:50,530
And you're gonna be here for a couple more.

389
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:51,870
- Oh, you're kidding me. - No.

390
00:17:51,870 --> 00:17:53,650
Nice meeting all of you.

391
00:17:56,160 --> 00:17:58,830
So, yeah, anyway, that's my boyfriend.

392
00:18:00,190 --> 00:18:02,830
He is really smart.

393
00:18:11,800 --> 00:18:13,830
I really like my saber-toothed cat.

394
00:18:13,900 --> 00:18:14,900
Thank you.

395
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:16,130
My pleasure.

396
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:19,360
Maybe after lunch, we can go to Marie Callender's

397
00:18:19,430 --> 00:18:20,700
And have some pie.

398
00:18:20,760 --> 00:18:22,160
I'd like it.

399
00:18:24,760 --> 00:18:26,760
This is turning out to be a perfect Saturday.

400
00:18:26,830 --> 00:18:28,830
Good.I'm glad.

401
00:18:31,660 --> 00:18:34,130
Oh, man. Did you see the way she smiled at me?

402
00:18:35,760 --> 00:18:37,600
Fine. Go ahead.

403
00:18:37,660 --> 00:18:39,460
No. This is our day.

404
00:18:39,530 --> 00:18:42,560
If you want to chase after her,chase after her.

405
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:46,800
Ah, who am I kidding? I wouldn't have a shot with a girl like that.

406
00:18:46,860 --> 00:18:48,310
Don't put yourself down.

407
00:18:48,310 --> 00:18:49,940
You're a very attractive man.

408
00:18:50,290 --> 00:18:51,620
- You think so?  - Yeah.

409
00:18:51,760 --> 00:18:53,570
Absolutely. It wouldn't kill you

410
00:18:53,570 --> 00:18:55,640
To take a Pilates class with me now and then,

411
00:18:55,640 --> 00:18:57,360
But you have a certain wiry appeal

412
00:18:57,430 --> 00:18:59,200
Yeah, well, it doesn't matter

413
00:18:59,260 --> 00:19:01,400
'cause she wasn't really smiling at me.

414
00:19:01,460 --> 00:19:04,100
Actually, in this case, I think she was.

415
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:04,760
Really?

416
00:19:04,890 --> 00:19:05,770
- Yeah. - Bye.

417
00:19:09,120 --> 00:19:10,700
What a douche.

